# Userscript TypeScript workspace

Invert IDE is not a normal TS project. Two **separate** pipelines share names like `scripts/<m>/main`. Changing one to fix a diagnostic usually breaks another.

Before any types/Monaco/import change: name the channel, name which files are in the program, then change one lever. Verify **own-script unexported types**, **`export type` auto-import from `scripts/<m>/types`**, and **`scripts/<m>/main` imports across script switches**.

## Two editor channels (do not collapse these)

| Channel | User action | How it becomes visible | Typical failure |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Own-script ambient** | Types pane with **no** top-level `import`/`export` | Active `types.d.ts` is a non-module `.d.ts` | TS2304 `Cannot find name 'Foo'` in **that** script |
| **ES modules** | `import { x } from "scripts/<m>/main"` or `.../types` | Real Monaco models at `file:///scripts/<m>/main.ts` and `.../types.d.ts` plus `package.json` extra libs | TS2307 `Cannot find module` |

`export` never means “also a page global”. Unexported types-pane names are **own-script only**. Other userscripts must import exported names.

```ts
// Channel A — active types pane, no import/export. Visible in this script's main only.
type PrettyStringifyOptions = { quoteStrings?: boolean };

// Channel B — import from another (or the same) userscript.
import type { PrettyStringifyOptions } from "scripts/pretty-stringify/types";
import { prettyStringify } from "scripts/pretty-stringify/main";
```

## Editor vs runtime (short split)

| | Editor (Monaco TS worker) | Runtime (page injection) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Source of truth | `WorkspaceService` models + package.json / CDN extra libs | Build worker emit + `prepareCompiledJavascript` |
| Type pane | IntelliSense only (not injected) | Ignored |
| `scripts/<m>/main` | Resolved via `baseUrl`/`paths` to `main.ts` models | Rewritten to `__INVERT_SHARED__` **only for Shared** |
| Closure | `getSharedImportModuleNames` on **`/main` only** | Injection plan from the same `/main` imports (`sharedScripts` is a save-time cache) |

Do not fix editor diagnostics by changing compiled-output rewrite, and do not “fix” injection by adding extra libs. Non-Shared `scripts/<m>/…` imports may typecheck in the editor and still fail at runtime — that is out of scope.

